    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: bbethwaite",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1738061",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: YES",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The XACML 2.0 core spec insists that the RequestContextPath attribute of AttributeSelector elements should be an xpath expression whose context node is the <xacml-context:Request> element, which seems to read that AttributeSelectors should be evaluated against the request context.  Things get hazier after comparison with the Sun implementation where there does not seem to be anything directly corresponding with the XACML context handler as illustrated in the XACML data-flow model - although the EvaluationContext seems pretty close.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "What this boils down to is my confusion over whether it is valid (according to the XACML spec) to interpret RequestContextPaths for AttributeSelectors as a compound string comprising \"Datastream ID\"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "underline"
           }
          ],
          "text": "\"Absolute XPath expression over Datastream\" such as, \"DC\"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": "\"/oai_dc:dc/dc:publisher\" which would be written in XACML as:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "<AttributeSelector RequestContextPath=\"DC/oai_dc:dc/dc:publisher\" DataType=\"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": "\"/>",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "and evaluate to a string bag of matching values.  I suspect that it is technically not allowable, however I can see no reasonable alternative that does not render the AttributeSelector redundant (such as an AttributeDesignator that performs the same operation).  Perhaps this is an unaddressed usage scenario with regard to the spec.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The advantage to including the datastream ID in the path is that it allows a narrowing down of the data required to fulfill the query and hence saves time in retrieval.  After receiving no response from the sunxacml mailing lists on the topic I have gone ahead and implemented as described above.  The resulting code is now in the custody of Chris and Bill who will hopefully do the commit for inclusion in the 2.3 release.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
